    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1020" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.61334/36: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-13T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Department advised that Ecuadorean Congress will make no provision for payment
                    of Association’s debts beyond those of local <pb facs="1021" n="897"
                        xml:id="pg897"/> banks and <hi rendition="#italic">vale</hi><anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d833-f1"/> holders regardless of promises made by the President to
                    special representative of Mercantile Bank of the Americas. You should make
                    discreet inquiry and inform Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d833-f1" n="34" xml:id="d833-f1-content">
                <p>Vouchers or receipts, having the character of promissory notes, for cacao
                    delivered to the Association by the growers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
